Frontend development is the part of web development that focuses on the user interface of a website. It includes everything that users can see and interact with, such as buttons, menus, images, text, forms, and page layouts. Frontend developers mainly use HTML, CSS, and JavaScript to create responsive and attractive web pages.

Backend development is the server-side part of a website. It is responsible for processing user requests, managing user authentication, handling business logic, and communicating with databases. Backend applications are commonly built using Java, Python, PHP, or Node.js.

Full-stack development combines both frontend and backend development. A full-stack developer has the knowledge to build an entire web application, including the user interface, server-side functionality, and database integration.

Example: On a website like Flipkart, the homepage, product images, and search option are part of the frontend. User login, payment processing, and order management are handled by the backend. A full-stack developer can develop and maintain both the frontend and backend of the application.



