When a user enters a website URL into a browser, the browser sends an HTTP request to the web server. The server receives the request and processes it. If the requested page needs data, the server retrieves the required information from the database. After processing the request, the server sends an HTTP response containing HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and other resources. Finally, the browser renders these files and displays the webpage to the user.



