A web development environment requires different tools to build and test websites efficiently. Visual Studio Code (VS Code) is used for writing and editing HTML, CSS, and JavaScript code. A web browser such as Google Chrome or Microsoft Edge is required to test websites. Node.js enables JavaScript to run outside the browser and supports modern development tools. Git is used for version control, while GitHub provides online storage and collaboration for projects. The Live Server extension automatically refreshes the browser whenever code changes are saved. A terminal or command prompt is also used to execute commands and manage project files.



