A web server is software or hardware that accepts requests from web browsers and delivers web pages or application data using HTTP or HTTPS. It works as a bridge between the client and the website.

Examples of commonly used web servers:
• Apache HTTP Server
• Nginx
• Microsoft IIS
• LiteSpeed Web Server
• Apache Tomcat

These web servers are widely used because they provide good speed, security, and reliability.



