A static website displays fixed content that remains the same for every visitor. It is generally built using HTML and CSS and does not require a database. A personal portfolio website is a common example of a static website.

A dynamic website generates content according to user input or data stored in a database. It uses server-side programming languages along with databases to provide personalized content. Examples include Facebook, YouTube, and Amazon.



