Five popular web browsers are Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Microsoft Edge, Apple Safari, and Opera.

Different browsers use different rendering engines to display web pages.

• Google Chrome – Blink
• Microsoft Edge – Blink
• Opera – Blink
• Mozilla Firefox – Gecko
• Apple Safari – WebKit

Rendering engines convert HTML, CSS, and JavaScript into the webpages users see on their screens. They differ in terms of speed, performance, browser compatibility, and support for web standards.



